      "instruction": "Return one impact-response-v4 JSON object. Follow the current coordination stage. For every finish, unit_outcome is required and must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null. Use evidence_insufficient when missing evidence prevents completing the task; keep explicit member outcomes. Discovery: read every frozen discovery_task member, propose one set of rule changes citing T refs from fixed_text_evidence. For finish return evidence_outcomes in member order using P/D refs, with outcome and a specific reason for each member. Declare analyzed only after its complete evidence was supplied; insufficient/unprocessed must remain explicit. Never copy group success to every member. Case stage: compare every R rule with complete case JSON, execution_notes and its original sources; return rule_ref/case_impacts, literal paths and actual values; evidence_outcomes is empty. All formal identities/positions/hashes belong to the server. For read return only fixed P/S/C/D reads, no outcome, candidates or evidence_outcomes. Keep negative conditions. Catalogs are metadata, not read evidence. All proposals pending review; deployment unknown. No test execution or official-record changes.",
